{"2092160": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Legend of Merchant 2", "steam_appid": 2092160, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Though this game carries the name of its predecessor, it doesn't have much in common with it and is a completely new game. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Note: This is not a trading game! Instead, it is about obtaining items for sale through your own collection, planting, and other functions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/546017f3345b46c273a372912b1b10da.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span>It will not support the Steam Workshop as I do not have the capability to do so.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The development team still consists of only me, and I cannot meet high expectations. You can try the free version before purchasing, and if the gameplay suits you, then buy it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each game I develop is the best I can do at the current stage, and I have invested a lot in this one.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/d58361b34ba467e711dbefe9c071e7fa.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span><strong>Gameplay</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It's very different from the challenging games I've developed in the past where bankruptcy leads to failure. This game is a pure collection-based casual simulation management game. There is no bankruptcy or time limit, so you can play it in a relaxed manner.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Of course, it lacks challenge and may bore players who enjoy challenges, as it cannot suit all players.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game does not have a “completion” concept, it is considered 'completed' when you no longer wish to play.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Resources can be obtained through farmland, cooking, or wild collection, and can be directly sold to shops or used to complete residents' commissions to earn money.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The prices of items will change once a week.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Although decision-making will affect the speed of making money, there is no need to be nervous, after all, there is no time limit, it's just a difference in speed.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Even if all the money is wasted, you can start over by working in the town's restaurant, so you don't have to worry about being in a dead end.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/32c564336d4a33448f068084babf68de.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span><strong>Controls</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Most operations are completed by clicking with the mouse (keyboard is used for collecting in the wild). It is also a turn-based game, and time will not pass without operation, so you can play it at ease.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlike ordinary farm games, there is no character to operate, but a conceptualized interface game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/023cec62fd90104b7c053e5f310bbdb0.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span><strong>Art</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All art is hand-drawn.  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/d4ddc7ec74b0ef464dd9bb008d0ae17f.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span><strong>music</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The background music is carefully selected high-quality paid licensed music.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/f3336d97a0877448ebf2a4699b906a49.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span><strong>Other</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is no investment, and I have always been developing games by myself at home.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Though this game carries the name of its predecessor, it doesn't have much in common with it and is a completely new game. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Note: This is not a trading game! Instead, it is about obtaining items for sale through your own collection, planting, and other functions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/546017f3345b46c273a372912b1b10da.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span>It will not support the Steam Workshop as I do not have the capability to do so.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The development team still consists of only me, and I cannot meet high expectations. You can try the free version before purchasing, and if the gameplay suits you, then buy it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each game I develop is the best I can do at the current stage, and I have invested a lot in this one.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2092160/extras/d58361b34ba467e711dbefe9c071e7fa.avif?t=1785829713\" width=128 height=128 /></span><strong>Gameplay</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It's very different from the challenging games I've developed in the past where bankruptcy leads to failure. This game is a pure collection-based casual simulation management 